jit: the MPYI/MACI immediate is a signed fraction

MPYI, MACI, MPYRI and MACRI carry a 24-bit immediate in the second opcode word,
and it is signed. The JIT path used it raw, so a negative coefficient was
multiplied out as a large positive one — 0xfcf669 (-0.0237) behaved as +1.976.
The interpreter path already sign-extends it.

--- a/source/dsp56kEmu/jitops_alu.cpp
+++ b/source/dsp56kEmu/jitops_alu.cpp
@@ -383,6 +383,14 @@ namespace dsp56k
 	{
 //		assert( sr_test(SR_S0) == 0 && sr_test(SR_S1) == 0 );
 
+		// MPYI/MACI/MPYRI/MACRI carry their operand as a 24-bit immediate in
+		// the second opcode word, and it is a SIGNED fraction. It arrives here
+		// raw, so a negative coefficient was multiplied out as a large positive
+		// one — 0xfcf669 (-0.0237) behaved as +1.976. The interpreter path is
+		// already correct; it sign-extends via immediateDataExt.
+		if (_s2.isImmediate() && !_s2Unsigned)
+			_s2.set(signextend<int32_t, 24>(static_cast<int32_t>(_s2.imm24())), DspValue::Immediate24);
+
 		AluRef d(m_block, ab, _accumulate, true);
 
 #ifdef HAVE_ARM64
